Z||000004||GTFiero1||10-19-2001||06:21 PM||||i posted about my 5hp go-kart earlier. i have "nitrous" well its not the same kind used on cars though. If you go to a pep boys or something go to where the feul additives are. the is a fuel additive made by NOS. it there is one in a blue can that increases it by 3point and one in a black can that increases it by 7points. dont get the black can or you may blow up the engine. just pour a little of this into the gas tank before you go riding it. What i did was ride it first to get the "feel" of it then added some of this. i felt a difference right away. i went easily 5-10mph faster. i also had the cylinder head professionally shaved 20 thousands of an inch for higher compression. if you dont have this yet doit. also a strait exhaust pipe. i cut a peice of led piping for this but you can buy them at <A HREF="http://www.kartworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kartworld.com</A>   also different air filters for better air flow. real Nitrous oxide would probably stack the rings real quick. somebody said that Compcams makes cams for these. i need to know there correct web site though<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000005||gt boy||10-20-2001||12:31 AM||||here is a little known fact...a company called Klotz makes a product call COXOC...it is very expensive about 80.oo a gallon.<P>it is basically a liquid oxygen product..it works wonders...sort of like "compression in a can".  it is very hard to detect in most racing sanctions when they test your fuel.<P>but don't use it in a high compession engine or boom!  it is designed for ...well...cheating in a stock racing class.<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
